{
  "configuration_id": "config_015",
  "reason": "The strongest result so far (config_039, multimodal scVI+ViT-L, multi-profile, transformer, weighted: 0.725) shows a ~7-point gain over the best RNA-only model (config_006: 0.653), but we have almost no information about the image modality's standalone contribution with ViT-L. The only image experiment (config_010, ResNet50 single-profile) was very weak (0.208) and used a different encoder. Config_015 (image-only, multi-profile, ViT-L, transformer) uses the same image encoder, profile setting, and aggregation as the best multimodal model, cleanly isolating the image modality's contribution. If image-alone performance is high (~0.60+), the multimodal gain is largely additive and future effort should focus on image-side improvements; if it is low (~0.30-0.40), the gain reflects true cross-modal synergy and we should prioritize fusion-strategy exploration. This single experiment resolves the largest remaining uncertainty about where the performance is coming from, directly guiding all subsequent design decisions under the limited budget."
}

